          {[
            ['Why is my LG DLE3400W running but not heating?', 'Several components can cause this symptom: the heating element, thermal fuse, thermostat, thermistor, power supply, or a wiring issue. The motor and drum can continue to operate normally while the heating circuit has a separate failure. Diagnosis is needed to identify which component failed.'],
            ['What heating element fits LG DLE3400W?', '5301EL1001J is a compatible heating element assembly listed for the LG DLE3400W. Verify part compatibility before ordering.'],
            ['What is LG part 5301EL1001J?', 'It is a heating element assembly used in the LG DLE3400W heating system. It converts electrical energy into radiant heat inside the dryer. When it fails, the dryer can still run the drum but produces no useful heat.'],
            ['Can an electric dryer tumble without heating?', 'Yes. The drum motor and the heating element are on separate circuits. The drum can tumble even when the heating element is not receiving power or has failed.'],
            ['Can a breaker issue cause a dryer to run but not heat?', 'Yes. An electric dryer requires a 240V circuit. If one leg of that circuit trips, the motor may still run while the heating element receives no power. A partially tripped breaker should be checked before replacing heating components.'],
            ['Can a clogged vent cause heating problems?', 'Yes. Restricted exhaust airflow can cause heat to build up inside the dryer. Safety devices are designed to open under overheating conditions, cutting off the heating system. A clogged vent can also cause a heating element to fail over time from repeated overheating.'],
